<p>
Welcome to the Chicago Booth Research Computing notes. This page provides
guidance for faculty, students, and staff using the HPC cluster for
quantitative research, coursework, and collaborative projects.
</p>

<p>
The Chicago Booth HPC environment supports statistical computing, machine
learning workflows, and large-scale data analysis. Jobs are scheduled through
Slurm and can be launched interactively via Jupyter or the desktop
application from the navigation menu.
</p>

<p>
For account access, allocation requests, and software environment questions,
contact the Chicago Booth IT Team at
<a href="mailto:helpdesk@chicagobooth.edu">helpdesk@chicagobooth.edu</a>.
</p>

<p>
When submitting jobs, select the appropriate partition and memory limits for
your workload. The debug partition is intended for short test runs; use the
compute partition for production analyses.
</p>
